    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nīdŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little nest.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ithacam illam, in asperrimis saxulis, tamquam
					nidulum, affixam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 44, 196</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 29, 2</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a place of
			retirement</i>: senectutis, Auct. ap. <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				6, 10, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opuscula mea, quia plurima evolaverunt de
					nidulo suo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 47, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
